From 3f0d320917b83d19421b61f294ceaf41631b90c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:03:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backgroundinfoloader: a stop that waited goes on where the
 interface stopped the loader meanwhile

StopThread() waits for a loader that is in the middle of a read, and on the thread of the
interface it keeps drawing meanwhile, with the busy dialog (6ff97e3):
CGUIDialogBusy::WaitOnEvent() runs the loop of the interface, which handles the messages
of the other threads (a window that a remote control or a script activates, the messages
of a scan) and so can close the window that waits, whose GUI_MSG_WINDOW_DEINIT stops the
same loader (GUIWindowVideoBase, GUIWindowMusicBase...). That inner StopThread() stops
and frees the thread, and the outer one, when its wait ends, called StopThread() on the
pointer it had just seen set: a null one, and Kodi crashed.

The thread is stopped and freed after the wait only where it is still there. A loader
loaded again from inside the wait is waited for, and stopped, as before.

Host test (outside the tree): t_reentry.sh builds the real BackgroundInfoLoader.cpp and
threads/ of the tree with stubs of the interface whose busy dialog runs, once, what the
loop of the interface would (a stop of the same loader; a stop and a new load), with
AddressSanitizer and UBSan: before, "member call on null pointer of type 'struct
CThread'"; after, both cases pass. The host test of the loader
(test_loader.cpp), written with the wait, passes as before.
---
 xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.cpp b/xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.cpp
index 5e0a632..19bebe5 100644
--- a/xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/BackgroundInfoLoader.cpp
@@ -245,8 +245,13 @@ void CBackgroundInfoLoader::StopThread()
   if (m_thread)
   {
     WaitForLoaderThread();
-    m_thread->StopThread();
-    m_thread.reset();
+    // Hades: the thread of the interface keeps drawing while it waits, and what it runs meanwhile
+    // (a window closed by a message) may have stopped this loader already, from the same thread
+    if (m_thread)
+    {
+      m_thread->StopThread();
+      m_thread.reset();
+    }
   }
   Reset();
   // no read of the loader is left to stop, and an item may be loaded again, by LoadItem()
-- 
